Wait, but hold on — the existing test names "queued run cancelled same tick" was AC1 of gh-846 (waste in queue). gh-848 changes it: cancelling a queued run leaves ghost check-runs. There's a tension: gh-846 wants the queued waste gone immediately; gh-848 says defer the cancel until materialization. Deferring means the queued run stays in the queue one more tick (waste continues) but no ghosts. Per gh-848, the ghost risk is worse (merge gate seized permanently vs. queue waste). AC3 of gh-848: twin-guard still suppresses duplicate dispatches — deferral is acceptable.

